==================================================
SPRINT 5A OBJECTIVE
==================================================

Implement ONLY:

AG-002 Context Integration Engine

Create a production-quality:

ContextIntegrationService

Its responsibility is to transform authorized RetrievalService
results into deterministic, safe, prioritized context suitable
for consumption by the future orchestration layer.

This is NOT an LLM summarizer.

This is NOT a vector search engine.

This is deterministic context assembly.

==================================================
1. SERVICE CONTRACT
==================================================

Create an interface-driven ContextIntegrationService.

It should accept existing retrieval results and context
configuration.

It should return a deterministic ContextIntegrationResponse.

Do not duplicate RetrievalService functionality.

Reuse existing:

- RetrievalService
- RetrievalResult
- MemoryRecord
- TokenEstimator
- sanitization
- priority definitions
- authorization/security infrastructure
- lifecycle filtering
- existing configuration patterns

==================================================
2. CONTEXT SECTIONS
==================================================

Build context sections according to existing AG-002 architecture.

Use existing memory types rather than inventing new ones.

Where appropriate support:

- USER
- PROJECT
- WORKSPACE
- ORGANIZATION
- CONVERSATION
- SESSION
- KNOWLEDGE_REFERENCE
- TEMPORARY

Do not invent memory types if they are not already defined.

Each generated section should have deterministic:

- section type
- priority
- records
- estimated tokens
- ordering
- truncation state

==================================================
3. DETERMINISTIC ORDERING
==================================================

Context ordering MUST be deterministic.

Use stable ordering based on existing metadata.

Recommended precedence:

1. section priority
2. memory priority
3. relevance score
4. timestamp/version
5. stable namespace/key identifier

Never depend on object insertion order accidentally.

The same input must produce the same output.

==================================================
4. PRIORITY PRESERVATION
==================================================

Existing priority levels:

CRITICAL
HIGH
MEDIUM
LOW

When budget is insufficient:

CRITICAL must be preserved whenever technically possible.

Then:

HIGH
MEDIUM
LOW

Lower priority information must never displace higher priority
information.

Record exactly what was:

- selected
- truncated
- excluded

==================================================
5. CONTEXT BUDGET
==================================================

Reuse the existing TokenEstimator.

Do NOT create another token estimation algorithm if one already
exists.

The final context must respect the configured context budget.

Test:

- normal budget
- tiny budget
- zero/invalid budget according to existing config policy
- large budget
- budget pressure

Ensure deterministic behavior.

==================================================
6. DEDUPLICATION
==================================================

Perform context-level deduplication using existing memory
identity semantics.

Prefer:

namespace + key

and respect version/relevance/priority according to the existing
architecture.

When duplicates exist:

- retain the best valid representation
- preserve CRITICAL information
- maintain deterministic behavior
- report deduplication statistics

Never mutate the source records.

==================================================
7. SAFE CONTEXT ASSEMBLY
==================================================

Context snippets must be safe.

Reuse the existing sanitization mechanism.

Sensitive information must never leak.

Test at minimum:

- apiKey
- password
- token
- secret
- credential
- pwd
- passphrase

Test nested metadata and mixed-case variants.

Do not rely only on formatter-level sanitization.

Sanitize at the context trust boundary.

==================================================
8. IMMUTABILITY
==================================================

The service MUST NOT mutate:

- RetrievalResult
- MemoryRecord
- metadata
- actor context
- nested objects

Add explicit immutability tests using deep snapshots.

